From: Hazel Smith <hazel@hazelesque.uk>
Subject: dynamic.list: export mimalloc public API (mi_*) symbols

musl's libc.so link uses `-Wl,--dynamic-list=dynamic.list` as a
positive allowlist: only symbols whose names match a pattern in
dynamic.list end up in the resulting DT_DYNSYM.  By default the
file lists only POSIX/glibc-compat globals (environ, malloc, free,
optarg, …); mimalloc's mi_* public API is not on it.

Add a single `mi_*;` glob.  This catches the 155 mi_*-prefixed
symbols at GLOBAL DEFAULT visibility in mimalloc.o (mimalloc's
documented public API, tagged `mi_decl_export = visibility("default")`
via the variant shim + mimalloc-allow-mi-export.patch).  The 66
internal mi_*-prefixed symbols are file-static (lowercase 't' in
nm output) and cannot be exported regardless of dynamic.list, so
the glob has no risk of leaking internals.

Hazelesque-only patch — main/musl/ deliberately doesn't expose
the mi_* surface.

diff --git a/dynamic.list b/dynamic.list
--- a/dynamic.list
+++ b/dynamic.list
@@ -38,4 +38,7 @@ __progname;
 __progname_full;

 __stack_chk_guard;
+
+/* hazelesque/musl-mimalloc-introspectable: mimalloc public API */
+mi_*;
 };
